sam: Heads-up 1 - small but customer-visible issue: after the retry middleware change the payments sample is delivering duplicate payment callbacks. Not a full outage but a few customers reported double charges.
ci-bot: deploy: js-sdk@2.3.0 rolled to staging (2026-03-30T19:10:02Z) :rocket:
nina: Can you paste a sanitized trace? key detail: is the receiver returning Retry-After and what format?
sam: Minimal trace (sanitized):
```
POST /payments/callback -> 429
Response headers: Retry-After: 2

client retry immediately -> 200 (duplicate payment processed)
```
leo: Quick debugging note: the Node patch used Number(ra) and then did `if (!wait) wait = 0` which treats "0" and NaN the same. That means whitespace or date strings fell back to immediate. Also our jitter util used signed gaussian which in rare tails returned negative jitter and subtracted from wait. Two bad combos.
dory: Also the sample-payments app does not set any idempotency header on outgoing callbacks. It's relying on the receiver to dedupe, which is brittle when retries are mis-tuned. We should default to adding an X-Redwood-Idempotency header (uuid4) and include it in the HMAC signature so receivers can safely dedupe.
nina: Suggested action items: 1) SDK parity: ensure all official SDKs parse Retry-After as either delta-seconds or HTTP-date (RFC7231) with a clear precedence. 2) Fix jitter to be strictly non-negative and additive (wait += uniform(0, jitter_ms)). 3) Default sample-apps and SDK helpers to attach X-Redwood-Idempotency unless explicitly opted-out. 4) Add CI lint to samples to fail if a webhook/callback path neither attaches idempotency header nor documents an explicit opt-out. 5) Emit telemetry metric duplicate_payment_webhook_count and alert thresholds.
leo: I'll open PRs for Node + Go: parsing fix + unit tests (numeric, IMF-fixdate, expired-date), jitter clamp, and a feature flag `honor_retry_after` default true for quick rollback. Example Node pseudo:
```js
const ra = res.headers['retry-after'];
let wait = 0;
if (/^\d+$/.test(ra)) wait = parseInt(ra,10);
else if (ra) {
  const t = Date.parse(ra);
  if (!Number.isNaN(t)) wait = Math.ceil((t - Date.now())/1000);
}
wait = Math.max(1, Math.min(wait, maxBackoffSeconds));
wait += Math.floor(Math.random()*jitterMs)/1000;
await sleep(wait*1000);
```
leo: And Go pseudo:
```go
ra := resp.Header.Get("Retry-After")
var wait time.Duration
if secs, err := strconv.Atoi(strings.TrimSpace(ra)); err == nil {
  wait = time.Duration(secs) * time.Second
} else if t, err := http.ParseTime(ra); err == nil {
  wait = time.Until(t)
}
if wait <= 0 { wait = time.Second }
wait += time.Duration(rand.Intn(jitterMs)) * time.Millisecond
time.Sleep(wait)
```
dory: I'll add the CI lint rule for samples and a small e2e `samples/payments/replay-test` that spins a fake receiver returning 429 with numeric and date Retry-After values and verifies the client waits and that a de-duplicating receiver sees a single processed idempotency key. I'll also update the payment sample to attach the idempotency header and include it in the signature helper.
nina: Telemetry: emit duplicate_payment_webhook_count with labels {sample_app, endpoint} and create a staging dashboard. Set alert if rate > 0.1% prod or >0.02% staging.
sam: Also add a short migration note for customers self-hosting older SDKs recommending upgrade and describing the idempotency header contract (header name, TTL 60s default, signature inclusion).
leo: Acceptance criteria for merges: unit tests for Retry-After parsing (secs + HTTP-date + expired-date), integration e2e with both header formats, samples attach idempotency header by default, CI lint in place, telemetry metric + dashboard.
dory: ETA: PRs today, CI lint + sample e2e tomorrow, staging smoke after lunch. I'll tag reviewers and link PRs here.
sam: Thanks team :thumbsup: keep this thread updated if any regressions show up.
